## Google — Protocol Buffers well-known types

`wasm/proto3_analyzer_bg.wasm` embeds the eleven well-known type definitions
that ship with [Protocol Buffers](https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protobuf) —
`any.proto`, `api.proto`, `descriptor.proto`, `duration.proto`, `empty.proto`,
`field_mask.proto`, `source_context.proto`, `struct.proto`, `timestamp.proto`,
`type.proto` and `wrappers.proto`, all under `google/protobuf/` — so that
`import "google/protobuf/…"` resolves, and hover and go-to-definition work on
the types they declare, with nothing else installed. The files are vendored at
`crates/proto3-analyzer/src/well_known/protos/` in this repository and are
compiled in with `include_str!`, their license headers intact.

They are not a crate dependency, so cargo-about cannot see them; this section is
written by hand, in `crates/proto3-analyzer/about.hbs`. They are distributed
under the BSD 3-Clause License:

